cell64lv2: search the LP64 SDK library directory first under -mlp64.

The lib_lv2 link spec adds -L $PS3DK/ppu/lib, where the ILP32 SDK
archives live.  The LP64 builds of liblv2, liblv2_stub, libc_stub and the
other SDK libraries are in $PS3DK/ppu/lib/lp64, but the spec never added
that directory, and a -L supplied by a spec is not adjusted for the
multilib.  An -mlp64 link that did not add -L .../lp64 itself (a plain
driver link, or a target that opts into -mlp64 under the ILP32 CMake
toolchain file) therefore took the ILP32 liblv2/stub archives and
produced a mixed-ABI executable.  The LP64 CMake toolchain file already
adds the directory, so whole-LP64 CMake projects were not affected.

Under -mlp64, add -L $PS3DK/ppu/lib/lp64 ahead of the flat directory.
The flat directory stays as a fallback, and an earlier user -L still takes
precedence, so a library that has no LP64 build is still found (as the
ILP32 archive); this fixes the default search, it does not reject every
mixed-ABI link.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
@@ -293,9 +293,12 @@
    compile time and resolves -L against $PS3DK/ppu/lib (which is where
    build-psl1ght.sh / build-sdk.sh install libsysbase, librt, liblv2,
    libc, and the reference SDK stub archives).  --start-group / --end-group
-   resolve circular deps between newlib, lv2 stubs, and libsysbase.  */
+   resolve circular deps between newlib, lv2 stubs, and libsysbase.
+   Under -mlp64 the LP64 archives live in $PS3DK/ppu/lib/lp64; that
+   directory must be searched first, or an LP64 link silently takes the
+   ILP32 liblv2/stub archives and produces a mixed-ABI executable.  */
 #define LIB_LV2_SPEC \
-  "-L %:getenv(PS3DK /ppu/lib) --start-group -lsysbase -lc -lrt -llv2 -llv2_stub -lc_stub --end-group"
+  "%{mlp64:-L %:getenv(PS3DK /ppu/lib/lp64)} -L %:getenv(PS3DK /ppu/lib) --start-group -lsysbase -lc -lrt -llv2 -llv2_stub -lc_stub --end-group"
 
 #define STARTFILE_LV2_SPEC \
   "lv2-crti.o%s crtbegin.o%s lv2-crt0.o%s lv2-sprx.o%s"
